WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:03.452
Date-based rules can change every day if we always
use the current

00:00:03.478 --> 00:00:09.043
system date For teaching and reproducible analysis
sometimes we

00:00:09.069 --> 00:00:13.375
want a fixed reference date In this example the
reference date is

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:18.645
August eleventh twenty twenty-six We look at
admissions in a thirty-day window

00:00:18.671 --> 00:00:24.447
and create a respiratory risk category The query
also joins admissions

00:00:24.459 --> 00:00:28.417
with patient information so we can use age in the
rule Run

00:00:28.443 --> 00:00:31.639
the example here in the browser and inspect the
admission dates and

00:00:31.665 --> 00:00:37.502
category You can copy it into pgAdmin as well
Because the reference

00:00:37.528 --> 00:00:40.711
date is fixed you and your classmates should get the
same cohort

00:00:40.737 --> 00:00:44.796
even if you run the example on different days Later
in a

00:00:44.822 --> 00:00:48.069
production system a dynamic date may be more
appropriate
